#
# Static signals common to all trailer branches.
#
# These signals always exist, also when no trailer is coupled. They are NOT marked
# "dynamic", so the broker never removes them. They are available to clients and to the
# broker before the dynamic signals of the trailer branch are resolved, and
# they carry the trigger signal and the input data of the branch actions.
#

IsConnected:
  datatype: boolean
  type: sensor
  description: Indicates if a trailer is coupled at this position. True = Trailer coupled. False = No trailer coupled.
  comment: Trigger signal of the events Connected and Disconnected of the trailer branch.
           A change from false to true makes the broker resolve the dynamic signals of the branch.
           A change from true to false makes the broker remove all dynamic signals of the branch.

Id:
  datatype: string
  type: sensor
  description: Unique identifier of the trailer coupled at this position, e.g. its VIN.
  comment: Shall be set before or together with IsConnected changing to true.
           Used by the action ResolveBranchByUri to build the URI of the trailer configuration.
           The identifier says which trailer is coupled, the trailer position (Trailer1 to Trailer5) does not.
